# Tests that no `ci.yml` filter selects, as of the commit that wrote this file.
#
# Written by `scripts/check_test_filter_coverage.py --write-baseline`, checked
# by the "Tests no filter selects (#408)" step of the `compile-tests` job.
# Entries are `<crate>::<test path>`.
#
# This file exempts the standing set so the guard fails only on ADDITIONS.
# It is allowed to shrink. Regenerating it to turn a red build green is the one
# edit that converts the guard back into decoration -- if the guard fires,
# either enrol the new test in a filter or justify the exemption in review.
#
# Seeded from CI, not from a developer machine: `cargo test -- --list` omits
# `#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]` tests everywhere except Linux, and those are
# exactly the entries whose absence made #171's gap invisible.
